{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept","id":956894,"title":"what happens if you kill the spirit of a concept?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-24T05:35:31-07:00","id":956894,"title":"what happens if you kill the spirit of a concept?","content":"to the concept i mean. <br /> <br /> so we know that if:<br /> i kill a minor bane of hatred, pretty much nothing will happen<br /> i kill a big bane of hatred the local area might be better for a while if only because of the absence of the banes actions<br /> i kill a really big bane of hatred then i might have purchased another dawn for gaia.<br /> i kill the maeljin incarna of hatred ...then the very concept will be severely weakened for some time. with actual effects on the world.<br /> so...what happens if i (by some miracle) kill angu the urge of hatred? i imagine that in the long run wyrm will eventually spawn a new one ,but what happens until then?<br /> especially since all the minor spirits of hatred will still exist(right?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:36:13-07:00","id":956957,"title":"","content":"I guess your thoughts are right.<br /> Even if one would get rid of Angu, and for a while, the whole concept of hatred would play a lesser role in the universe, it would eventually get back to normal - unless you repeat the cycle often enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:00:48-07:00","id":957208,"title":"","content":"yes but what i do not understand is this. what happens to lower spirits if you remove a higher one?<br /> <br /> for instance let's say the spirit(propably an incarna) of a major city is killed. now assuming for the sake of the experiment that we prevent any other spirit from filling the gap, is causality itsself altered so that the city(and many of its spirits ) are destroyed eventually.<br /> <br /> such as, a big economic hit, an earthquake or even a sudden desire to move away. sort of like what happens in the book &quot;it&quot; after pennywise is destroyed<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:27:34-07:00","id":957229,"title":"","content":"Looking at what has happened to Totems who fall or otherwise go away, their Broods tend to get adopted into other Totem's Broods.<br /> I would assume the same thing happens here. If A City Totem is destroyed of even significantly weakened, there is a good chance that it's lower spirits go with it, or are adopted by other similarly aligned Totems, like Rat or Cockroach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T15:35:34-07:00","id":957233,"title":"","content":"I actually think that the killer of a major spirit of a concept becomes a major spirit of that concept. To weaken a convept, imprison the spirit, killing it just makes you into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T16:52:23-07:00","id":957270,"title":"","content":"That's how it works for Maeljin specifically. There is no reason that if you kill New York, that you would become the new City Father/Mother. Or Fenris or any other Incarna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T18:18:39-07:00","id":957302,"title":"","content":"If you kill an Incarna, it inconveniences the Celestine over the Incarna, who has to deputize or create a new spirit to fill the fallen Incarna's place. If a Celestine dies, the thing in question goes with it, lost forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T19:29:31-07:00","id":957334,"title":"","content":"Just out of curiosity, where is that written? Not that it matters that much, since killing a Celestine requires Death Star levels of power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:12:57-07:00","id":957362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept#post956894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">to the concept i mean.<br /> <br /> so we know that if:<br /> i kill a minor bane of hatred, pretty much nothing will happen<br /> i kill a big bane of hatred the local area might be better for a while if only because of the absence of the banes actions<br /> i kill a really big bane of hatred then i might have purchased another dawn for gaia.<br /> i kill the maeljin incarna of hatred ...then the very concept will be severely weakened for some time. with actual effects on the world.<br /> so...what happens if i (by some miracle) kill angu the urge of hatred? i imagine that in the long run wyrm will eventually spawn a new one ,but what happens until then?<br /> especially since all the minor spirits of hatred will still exist(right?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Here's my take on it.<br /> <br /> I think of concept spirits more like amplifiers than sources, most of the time. You could kill every single spirit of hatred, from the weakest to the strongest, but the concept of hate would still exist in the physical world amongst mortals because what happens between the worlds takes time to resonate through to the other side. What killing/neutralizing all of those spirits would do is disempower hatred; and instead of lathering it, ramping it up, and precipitating it, it would make it possible to maybe eradicate practiced hatred in a more mundane way, over time.<br /> <br /> Spirits are a bit like drugs in their relation to people, I think. Spirits of concepts are something that reinforce reactions and behaviors related to them, which in turns breeds more of them or otherwise feeds them stronger. So cutting off the spirit of that concept won't erase it from the person it has been affecting, but it'll remove a layer of influence that was preventing the person from acting otherwise, and then from there you can start a 12-step with the person. It opens the opportunity, the possibility. but not the assurance.<br /> <br /> The problem with trying to eradicate the concept of hatred isn't just the spirits, though. You still have to deal with the concept existing in the real world, in memories, in behaviors, in active experiences that can easily spark and rebirth it. The nature of it is very cyclical and killing the spirit is only one part of an immense process. because slaying the spirit doesn't remove all those other lingering parts of the concept. A room with a gas leak is still full of gas even once you cut off the supply and all.<br /> <br /> That's a really heavy situation and seems pretty futile, I'm sure. But if some people were really dedicated to tackling the issue of hatred in the world, it would be necessary to combat (in some way, whether with actual fighting or some other Theurgy wooginess) the related spirits in order to level the playing field a bit. A lot of the work would have be done in the Tellurian, both to weaken the spirits you'd need to combat, and also to lay a foundation of the work actually sticking.<br /> <br /> As for what happens when you've slain Lord Steel, or managed to bind or somehow destroy Abhorra itself? I think the events that play out following would have to weigh in heavily. Someone would have to rise to the occasion of promoting hatred as an ideal and be promoted to to fill that vacancy. I don't think it would happen automatically and as a matter of course. I think if a campaign against hate was concerted enough, the 'promotion' could be stalled for quite a while. Again, that wouldn't mean that hate would just suddenly cease to exist in the actions and psyche of physical beings, but there'd be nothing to feed upon it, or feed into it for a while. Of course, this working on the premise that the slayers themselves have somehow managed to purge themselves of all their hatred, including for the Urge Wyrm they miraculously managed to subdue, and didn't secretly become its new manifestation in the process. Even the more centered of Children of Gaia, Stargazer, or the like, would have a great deal of trouble with this, I think, and that's probably the main hitch in a campaign like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":2810,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","user":"Yakecen-Sings","date":". 08-24-2016, 11:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T23:46:11-07:00","id":957436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=957208#post957208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yes but what i do not understand is this. what happens to lower spirits if you remove a higher one?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say:<br /> Short term, nothing happens. The spirits are self aware, not required to have an higher one and therefore continue to do their daily work..<br /> For mid or long term analysis it depends on what concept is affected, but if the concept doesn't simply disappear a new higher spirit will form, either out of it's own or by some being merging into that position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T07:28:12-07:00","id":957611,"title":"","content":"I think that the spirits are a reflection of the concept, not the concept itself. Killing off the Incarna of Hate will only get rid of a spiritual entity that seeks to promote hate, but hatred will still exist in the hearts of men and will cause them to act savagely. At best, the Incarnation is replaced by a spirit less effective at organization. At worst, the Incarnation is replaced by a spirit more effective at organization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:45:24-07:00","id":957746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=957611#post957611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that the spirits are a reflection of the concept, not the concept itself. Killing off the Incarna of Hate will only get rid of a spiritual entity that seeks to promote hate, but hatred will still exist in the hearts of men and will cause them to act savagely. At best, the Incarnation is replaced by a spirit less effective at organization. At worst, the Incarnation is replaced by a spirit more effective at organization.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incarna are reflections of concepts and things, it is true, but Celestines are literally the thing they represent. Luna is the Moon- if something were to happen to her, catastrophic destruction would befall the mundane moon in orbit, and vice-versa. Rorg has not been doing well since his physical form broke up.<br /> <br /> Not that destroying a Celestine is generally within the scope of a given game, but slaying one would certainly alter the physical world in a major way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:01:50-07:00","id":957758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=957746#post957746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incarna are reflections of concepts and things, it is true, but Celestines are literally the thing they represent. Luna is the Moon- if something were to happen to her, catastrophic destruction would befall the mundane moon in orbit, and vice-versa. Rorg has not been doing well since his physical form broke up.<br /> <br /> Not that destroying a Celestine is generally within the scope of a given game, but slaying one would certainly alter the physical world in a major way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think of it this way: it's probably as difficult to kill a Celestine as it is to destroy the thing it represents. Luna, for instance, would require enough force equivalent to reducing the Moon to gravel.<br /> <br /> Celestines, ergo, are pretty damn hard to kill. Thankfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T12:36:51-07:00","id":957777,"title":"","content":"And destroying Helios would take orders of magnitude more force than destroying Luna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:04:57-07:00","id":957792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=957334#post957334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just out of curiosity, where is that written? Not that it matters that much, since killing a Celestine requires Death Star levels of power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beyond Death Star, really, and in Umbra Revised and W20 Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T13:11:21-07:00","id":957796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=957777#post957777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And destroying Helios would take orders of magnitude more force than destroying Luna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. At that point though you are comparing how hard it would be to destroy 2 completely unstatted beings.<br /> <br /> In any case, in a Werewolf game, Luna is described has a lot more Spiritual &quot;oomph&quot; as it were than Helios. So while it is theoretically easier to destroy the moon than the sun, that has little to do with the spiritual beings they are in the Umbra. Again though, this is a moot argument because both are effectively invincible unless the story says otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T11:54:33-07:00","id":958320,"title":"","content":"werewolf explicitly says that if the spirit of something dies then the object dies as well. in case of concepts however i think that(i know this is more mage than werewolf but it's the only way to make sense of it) they have an inertial due to being in place for so long.thus the the triat member in question would have time to&quot; heal&quot;. and regrow that part. e.g hatred<br /> <br /> but what would be funny is killing a celestine that belongs partially to all three of them<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T12:56:52-07:00","id":958367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=957796#post957796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really. At that point though you are comparing how hard it would be to destroy 2 completely unstatted beings.<br /> <br /> In any case, in a Werewolf game, Luna is described has a lot more Spiritual &quot;oomph&quot; as it were than Helios. So while it is theoretically easier to destroy the moon than the sun, that has little to do with the spiritual beings they are in the Umbra. Again though, this is a moot argument because both are effectively invincible unless the story says otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it is a bit like any other argument of that scale. It really does not matter if it takes one million metric tons of antimatter or one trillion metric tons of antimatter, it will never happen because no one can create (or store) enough antimatter to reach even a trillionth of the lower scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T20:00:53-07:00","id":958576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=958320#post958320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">werewolf explicitly says that if the spirit of something dies then the object dies as well.</div> </div> </div> </div> Although what &quot;dying&quot; constitutes is circumstantial, I'd say. If a spirit residing in a particular tree died, that's pretty straight forward and the tree just dies also, and any things the tree provided either physically or spiritually would cease.<br /> <br /> If Luna somehow died, the moon wouldn't just spontaneously explode. Instead, I imagine something like:<br /> Shifters who get their boons from Luna would no longer them, such as Rage, moon-taught Gifts, moon-related Fetishes would probably stop functioning, maybe silver would stop being a vulnerability. All of the mystical aspects of the moon would become disempowered. Regard of the moon in spirituality would probably start to fade, and even mundane regard of it would follow suit. No one would care that we landed on the moon, because who gives a shit about the moon anyway. It would just become an inert lump of space rock tidal locked with us, not really worthy of much thought, and &quot;without&quot; spiritual significance.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" ><img itemprop=\"image\" data-align=\"center\" data-linktype=\"1\" data-linkurl=\"https://www.thecyberrecord.net/quests\" data-size=\"full\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://i.imgur.com/iZ3OWzG.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment align_center\" /></a></div><br /> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2810-yakecen-sings","name":"Yakecen-Sings","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2810_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T22:57:39-07:00","id":958616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yakecen-Sings</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/956894-what-happens-if-you-kill-the-spirit-of-a-concept?p=958576#post958576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Although what &quot;dying&quot; constitutes is circumstantial, I'd say. If a spirit residing in a particular tree died, that's pretty straight forward and the tree just dies also, and any things the tree provided either physically or spiritually would cease.<br /> <br /> If Luna somehow died, the moon wouldn't just spontaneously explode. Instead, I imagine something like:<br /> Shifters who get their boons from Luna would no longer them, such as Rage, moon-taught Gifts, moon-related Fetishes would probably stop functioning, maybe silver would stop being a vulnerability. All of the mystical aspects of the moon would become disempowered. Regard of the moon in spirituality would probably start to fade, and even mundane regard of it would follow suit. No one would care that we landed on the moon, because who gives a shit about the moon anyway. It would just become an inert lump of space rock tidal locked with us, not really worthy of much thought, and &quot;without&quot; spiritual significance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that the mundane aspects of the moon would remain, it would simply loose all its magical 'Oomph'. I mean, the moon is still there, that fact we landed on it is a triumph of science, and it still looks pretty in the night sky. So the technocracy and the weaver probably won't give a collective shit, but the supernatural world would be devastated.<br /> <br /> Also having the an entity killing of celestines and in doing so systematically wiping out magic would be one hell of a terrifying concept to any non-mundane creature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T23:07:37-07:00","id":958617,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm pretty sure that if there's something killing Celestines, there's bigger problems than the nuances of the effects psyche with sudden absence of such a prominent spirit would cause, anyway. Too spooky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\"><a href=\"http://thecyberrecord.net\" target=\"_blank\">The Cyber Record</a> is on the </span></b><a href=\"http://geomid.network\" target=\"_blank\"><b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Geomid.Network</span></b></a><br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:verdana\">Activism is Gaian praxis</span></b></div> <div align=\"right\"> <div class=\"img_align_center_wrapper\"><a href=\"ht